      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is a concise and professional section suitable for your field technician guide. This structure balances necessary information with readability, keeping the complexity score manageable.\n\n**Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor Quick Start**\n\nThe Nexus-7 operates on a 5V DC power input via USB-C and functions between -10C and 50C. For initial setup, connect the unit to the Nexus Hub and execute the `nexus-sync` command in the terminal until the LED shows a steady green blink. To finalize installation, secure the sensor using an M3 screw into the designated bracket.\n\n**Safety and Operation Notes:**\n*   Never submerge the sensor in liquid or exceed the 5V power limit.\n*   During calibration, ensure the sensor is held 10cm from a flat surface and avoid direct high-intensity UV exposure.\n*   Confirm sensor status by observing the LED: Solid Green indicates active status, Red signals an error or lack of power.",
      "source": "target",
